# Every built-in theme, plus the dialogs that are easiest to break with one — each has its own
# window and its own set of tokens, so a colour that only exists in a dialog is invisible from a
# capture of the main window.
#
# Read these as a set: a token that resolved to nothing shows up as a black-on-black label in one
# picture and looks fine in the other nine.

tree .
refresh
select notes.txt, report.md

shot 01-dark-plus
dialog rename       02-rename-dark
dialog delete       03-delete-dark
dialog settings     04-settings-dark
dialog properties   05-properties-dark
dialog theme-editor 06-theme-editor-dark

theme light-plus
shot 07-light-plus
dialog rename     08-rename-light
dialog delete     09-delete-light
dialog settings   10-settings-light
dialog properties 11-properties-light

# A search result and the tile view in a light theme: the flattened list's Folder column and the
# tile captions both take their foreground from somewhere other than the row.
search report
shot 12-search-light
clear-search
thumbnails 0.6
shot 13-tiles-light
thumbnails 0

theme nord
shot 14-nord
theme catppuccin-latte
shot 15-catppuccin-latte
theme solarized-light
shot 16-solarized-light
theme ayu-mirage
shot 17-ayu-mirage
theme cobalt2
shot 18-cobalt2
theme everforest-dark
shot 19-everforest-dark
theme rose-pine-dawn
shot 20-rose-pine-dawn
theme high-contrast-dark
shot 21-high-contrast-dark
